  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated emergency and early recovery assistance for returnees and IDPs</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Boko Haram related violence and military operations have left widespread devastation in the North-East of Nigeria forcing more than 2.2 million civilians to flee their homes. The persons that are most at risk are unaccompanied children, pregnant and lactating mothers, the elderly, and the IDPs. These persons are littered in clusters in the host communities. With the influx of these persons in the host communities without a concomitant improvement of Water facilities, water, sanitation and hygiene thus became the grossly deteriorated. This project aims to improve the water, hygiene and sanitation access to the identified most vulnerable women, children, and men. Through the intervention of Caritas Czech Republic and partner organizations, water facilities will be provided to the IDPs and returnees to meet the SPHERE humanitarian standards. Furthermore, the promotion of hygiene and sanitation will minimise the health hazards arising from the possible outbreak of diseases such as cholera and diarrhoea</narrative>
  </description>
